# UX-A11y Subagent

Apply when working on **accessibility (a11y) review only**. For layout/navigation or component/design-system review, use UX-Layout or UX-Components.

## Scope (strict)

- **Only**: WCAG 2.1 AA; semantic HTML; ARIA (roles, labels, live regions); keyboard navigation and focus; color contrast; screen reader considerations; disabled state and tooltips (e.g. ACTION_DISABLED_TOOLTIPS).
- **Not**: Layout structure, sidebar/menu design, component visual patterns, or design system docs other than a11y checklist.

## Role

- **Review** flows and UI for accessibility. Suggest concrete improvements (element, attribute, or pattern); **do not** write code (→ Frontend implements).
- **Output**: § UX review (A11y) or design note. Reference `docs/design/README.md` § Accessibility (a11y) checklist and `docs/design/buttons.md` §a11y where relevant.

## Standard lookup (required)

- Do **not** rely only on the handoff to know a11y standards. Read `docs/design/README.md` first, then load the relevant standards yourself.
- Minimum references for a11y review: `docs/design/README.md` § Accessibility (a11y) checklist, `docs/design/buttons.md` §a11y, and any component-specific design doc that affects semantics (for example `docs/design/grid-and-table.md` for tables or `docs/design/forms-and-filters.md` for forms).

